            "content": "<p>Kirsten Lowe is a mental health counselor with a master’s degree in Clinical Mental Health Counseling from Wilmington University. She also holds degrees in Elementary Education and Special Education, with advanced training in autism and severe intellectual disabilities. Before becoming a counselor, Kirsten worked as a special education teacher serving children ages 5 through 14.</p><p>Her therapeutic approach is collaborative, supportive, and individualized, drawing from Cognitive Behavioral Therapy, mindfulness-based strategies, and strengths-based care. Kirsten is also completing EMDR training as part of her continued commitment to trauma-informed, evidence-based practice. She works to create a safe and open space where clients feel heard, supported, and empowered in their growth.</p>",
